text.section:
Insurance policies carried pursuant to subsection A must provide that:

Each proprietary lessee is an insured person under the policy with respect to liability arising out of his interest in the common elements or membership in the association;


The insurer waives its right to subrogation under the policy against any proprietary lessee or member of his household;


No act or omission by any proprietary lessee, unless acting within the scope of his authority on behalf of the association, will void the policy or be a condition to recovery under the policy; and


If, at the time of a loss under the policy, there is other insurance in the name of a proprietary lessee covering the same risk covered by the policy, the association's policy provides primary insurance.
